{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel","id":1488269,"title":"Eye of Hazimel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-28T11:18:26-07:00","id":1488269,"title":"Eye of Hazimel","content":"The legendary artifact Eye of Hazimel never had its powers stated. How would you guys make it work? What powers should it have and, of course, side effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T12:12:32-07:00","id":1488274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel#post1488269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The legendary artifact Eye of Hazimel never had its powers stated. How would you guys make it work? What powers should it have and, of course, side effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my write-up, inspired by the Hand and Eye of Vecna.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Eye of Hazmiel</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Eye of Hazmiel creates a psychic link between the user who implants it in their eye socket and the torporous Methuselah, Hazmiel, inside India. Wielders gain access to Hazmiel's Disciplines like Chimestry, Vicissitude, Koldunic Sorcery, and other powers. Why Hazmiel has so much access to Tzimisce abilities can be summarized as, &quot;He's 10,000 years old. He has access to whatever he wants to.&quot; Unfortunately, while an impressive gain, the Eye of Hazmiel provides the sleeping ancient the ability to dominate or possess the wearer at will.<br /> <br /> As Leopold demonstrates, the Eye of Hazmiel also causes a horrifying degeneration of the consciousness of the wielder with the wearer losing one point of Humanity per week unless they make a successful resisted will check against Hazmiel (good luck with that). Wightdom is inevitable, though the Wight maintains access to all of the abilities provided by the Eye. This has resulted in a couple of wielders becoming added to the Red List. A Ravnos of Hazmiel's lineage or a Kindred sorcerer of sufficient preparation can hold back the degeneration for a time, though remains subject to Hazmiel's commands.<br /> <br /> It is believed that Hazmiel used to use the Eye as a &quot;gift&quot; to his primary servants but without a compact, that it leaves only a trail of miserable insane godlike Kindred in their week.</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-28-2022, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T12:29:21-07:00","id":1488276,"title":"","content":"Not much is known about Hazimel, only that he originated in India and was a rebellious childe that left his sire after an undefined period of time. Rumors tell that he was a stonemason in life who used his Eye as a method of control over various rulers.<br /> The Ravnos claim that he was born &quot;far to the North&quot; and served originally as a guardian of a goddess dedicated to combating the asuratizayya (Kuei-jin).<br /> The asuratizayya eventually retaliated against her by turning Hazimel against her, causing him to kill her.<br /> Insane with grief, he ripped out his own eye and fled into the mountains, where he was discovered by Zapathasura. When the Antediluvian offered him vengeance, Hazimel accepted, forsaking his name for the title &quot;Rakshasa&quot;. He is said to have bared his Eye as a nazar (A nazar - word deriving from Arabic, meaning sight, surveillance, attention, and other related concepts - is an eye-shaped amulet believed to protect against the evil eye. It is commonly believed that the evil eye can be given in the guise of a compliment, signifying its connection to the destructive power of envy (for one\u2019s wealth, beauty etc.). Amulets such as the Nazar are used in accordance with common sayings such as &quot;an eye for an eye&quot;, where another eye can be used to protect the recipient of the malefic gaze.The evil eye causes its victim to become unwell the next day, unless a protective phrase such as &quot;With the will of God&quot; (&quot;InshAllah&quot; in Arabic) is recited. Among adherents of Hinduism and Islam in South Asia, when a mother observes that her child is being excessively complimented, it is common for them to attempt to neutralize the effects of the evil eye (nazar utarna) by &quot;holding red chilies in one hand and circling the child's head a few times, then burning the chilies), which allowed him to see through falsehoods.<br /> The Karavalanisha Vrana records that the Rakshasa became war-weary and confronted his sire with this. The two clashed and the Rakshasa became Zapathasura's second-greatest enemy, supposed to have cast his lot with one of his greater nemeses like Ennoia. In some versions of the story, he left India for either Africa (as progenitor of the Kinyonyi) or the Middle Kingdom, while in others, Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent.<br /> Other sources claim that he was betrayed by Ravana after the latter turned to infernalism, because his eye could see through his deceptions.<br /> <br /> Various powers could be granted by the Eye it seems. <br /> When someone posess the Eye I give him a dircet line to the imprisoned/Toprid Rakshasa, who either quietly see thrugh the eye or try to influence the bearer via dreams/nightmares <br /> Granting Auspex 5-7 and limited protection against Infernal powers, a 6th sense like precognition and Highlander-like feeling when an infernalist, Kuei-jin or someone who is hiding via magical means or discipline is around.<br /> Somtimes immunity to Chimestry and other reality warping powers. <br /> The Eye sometimes acts as a beacon wich atracts the attention of the yama king Ravana and his servants when I'm in a particilurly evil mood<br /> <br /> But to be honest, rarely use it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T13:31:40-07:00","id":1488278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488274#post1488274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's my write-up, inspired by the Hand and Eye of Vecna.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Eye of Hazmiel</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Eye of Hazmiel creates a psychic link between the user who implants it in their eye socket and the torporous Methuselah, Hazmiel, inside India. Wielders gain access to Hazmiel's Disciplines like Chimestry, Vicissitude, Koldunic Sorcery, and other powers. Why Hazmiel has so much access to Tzimisce abilities can be summarized as, &quot;He's 10,000 years old. He has access to whatever he wants to.&quot; Unfortunately, while an impressive gain, the Eye of Hazmiel provides the sleeping ancient the ability to dominate or possess the wearer at will.<br /> <br /> As Leopold demonstrates, the Eye of Hazmiel also causes a horrifying degeneration of the consciousness of the wielder with the wearer losing one point of Humanity per week unless they make a successful resisted will check against Hazmiel (good luck with that). Wightdom is inevitable, though the Wight maintains access to all of the abilities provided by the Eye. This has resulted in a couple of wielders becoming added to the Red List. A Ravnos of Hazmiel's lineage or a Kindred sorcerer of sufficient preparation can hold back the degeneration for a time, though remains subject to Hazmiel's commands.<br /> <br /> It is believed that Hazmiel used to use the Eye as a &quot;gift&quot; to his primary servants but without a compact, that it leaves only a trail of miserable insane godlike Kindred in their week.</span></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow! Nice! That's a great write-up, I'm probably going to use in one of my stories. So, basically by your write up, the wearer becomes a plot device, right? I'm wondering the risks in case a PC gets it in the story I'm going to write, so that's the main reason I asked about the powers it confers. You know, when there's a power artifact in game, players are always going to try to get it lol. In any case, I really loved the write-up. For the statistics I think, by your writing, it's supposed to give access to level 9 in those 3 disciplines, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T13:33:24-07:00","id":1488279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488276#post1488276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much is known about Hazimel, only that he originated in India and was a rebellious childe that left his sire after an undefined period of time. Rumors tell that he was a stonemason in life who used his Eye as a method of control over various rulers.<br /> The Ravnos claim that he was born &quot;far to the North&quot; and served originally as a guardian of a goddess dedicated to combating the asuratizayya (Kuei-jin).<br /> The asuratizayya eventually retaliated against her by turning Hazimel against her, causing him to kill her.<br /> Insane with grief, he ripped out his own eye and fled into the mountains, where he was discovered by Zapathasura. When the Antediluvian offered him vengeance, Hazimel accepted, forsaking his name for the title &quot;Rakshasa&quot;. He is said to have bared his Eye as a nazar (A nazar - word deriving from Arabic, meaning sight, surveillance, attention, and other related concepts - is an eye-shaped amulet believed to protect against the evil eye. It is commonly believed that the evil eye can be given in the guise of a compliment, signifying its connection to the destructive power of envy (for one\u2019s wealth, beauty etc.). Amulets such as the Nazar are used in accordance with common sayings such as &quot;an eye for an eye&quot;, where another eye can be used to protect the recipient of the malefic gaze.The evil eye causes its victim to become unwell the next day, unless a protective phrase such as &quot;With the will of God&quot; (&quot;InshAllah&quot; in Arabic) is recited. Among adherents of Hinduism and Islam in South Asia, when a mother observes that her child is being excessively complimented, it is common for them to attempt to neutralize the effects of the evil eye (nazar utarna) by &quot;holding red chilies in one hand and circling the child's head a few times, then burning the chilies), which allowed him to see through falsehoods.<br /> The Karavalanisha Vrana records that the Rakshasa became war-weary and confronted his sire with this. The two clashed and the Rakshasa became Zapathasura's second-greatest enemy, supposed to have cast his lot with one of his greater nemeses like Ennoia. In some versions of the story, he left India for either Africa (as progenitor of the Kinyonyi) or the Middle Kingdom, while in others, Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent.<br /> Other sources claim that he was betrayed by Ravana after the latter turned to infernalism, because his eye could see through his deceptions.<br /> <br /> Various powers could be granted by the Eye it seems.<br /> When someone posess the Eye I give him a dircet line to the imprisoned/Toprid Rakshasa, who either quietly see thrugh the eye or try to influence the bearer via dreams/nightmares<br /> Granting Auspex 5-7 and limited protection against Infernal powers, a 6th sense like precognition and Highlander-like feeling when an infernalist, Kuei-jin or someone who is hiding via magical means or discipline is around.<br /> Somtimes immunity to Chimestry and other reality warping powers.<br /> The Eye sometimes acts as a beacon wich atracts the attention of the yama king Ravana and his servants when I'm in a particilurly evil mood<br /> <br /> But to be honest, rarely use it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems nice as well, although not nearly as powerful as I thought it was supposed to be to make Xaviar think he was dealing with the power of an Antediluvian (and Xaviar was no kid so to speak lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T14:50:57-07:00","id":1488284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488278#post1488278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow! Nice! That's a great write-up, I'm probably going to use in one of my stories. So, basically by your write up, the wearer becomes a plot device, right? I'm wondering the risks in case a PC gets it in the story I'm going to write, so that's the main reason I asked about the powers it confers. You know, when there's a power artifact in game, players are always going to try to get it lol. In any case, I really loved the write-up. For the statistics I think, by your writing, it's supposed to give access to level 9 in those 3 disciplines, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. You can probably use others but it's not like you'd need others.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you have the PCs get the Eye of Hazmiel and put it in their eye, I would tell them this:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Storyteller to Player</b>: Okay, there's now two ways this story can go. You have the option of cutting the eye out before your Humanity drops to zero and that will take all the Frodo-esque struggle you can. If that's how you want to roleplay it, that's a great idea. The other option, and these aren't completely mutually exclusive, you can go on a power-game spree of using the Eye against your enemies and acting like the Dragon Reborn for a time. Think of it as an invincibility star. The thing is that either this will be your roleplaying your character to their tragic but awesome demise OR you can try to deal with the aftermath of whatever happens once you pry out the eye. Which might include, &quot;Oh yeah, I killed the Prince, slaughtered a bunch of my friends, and turned the Archon into a flesh-art piece. I'm now dead unless I fake my death and the Kindred have a lot of experience with investigating that.&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> I actually did this once with the Player in a solo game where I jumped ahead a year's game time and they had no idea why the entirety of the city was now different as well as them hated by everyone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T17:15:39-07:00","id":1488294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488284#post1488284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. You can probably use others but it's not like you'd need others.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you have the PCs get the Eye of Hazmiel and put it in their eye, I would tell them this:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Storyteller to Player</b>: Okay, there's now two ways this story can go. You have the option of cutting the eye out before your Humanity drops to zero and that will take all the Frodo-esque struggle you can. If that's how you want to roleplay it, that's a great idea. The other option, and these aren't completely mutually exclusive, you can go on a power-game spree of using the Eye against your enemies and acting like the Dragon Reborn for a time. Think of it as an invincibility star. The thing is that either this will be your roleplaying your character to their tragic but awesome demise OR you can try to deal with the aftermath of whatever happens once you pry out the eye. Which might include, &quot;Oh yeah, I killed the Prince, slaughtered a bunch of my friends, and turned the Archon into a flesh-art piece. I'm now dead unless I fake my death and the Kindred have a lot of experience with investigating that.&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> I actually did this once with the Player in a solo game where I jumped ahead a year's game time and they had no idea why the entirety of the city was now different as well as them hated by everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's certainly good advice to deal with such situation and yes, I guess there's probably not any need to use anything else if one has access Chimerstry 9 lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T18:56:58-07:00","id":1488299,"title":"","content":"Hazimel created the eye as gift to antideluvians to expand their domian. Hazimel didn't have tons of visscitude or kokdunic sorcery. It's far more likely that the Tzimisce Antideluvian tapped into the artifact when Leopold had it and why he was drawn to New York. Using him as a vessel for it's plans. It's the reason why Leopold starts building his own cathedral of flesh in new York","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:00:03-07:00","id":1488300,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the guy who went all crazy with the Eye a Tremere, instead of a Tzimisce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:00:49-07:00","id":1488301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488299#post1488299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hazimel created the eye as gift to antideluvians to expand their domian. Hazimel didn't have tons of visscitude or kokdunic sorcery. It's far more likely that the Tzimisce Antideluvian tapped into the artifact when Leopold had it and why he was drawn to New York. Using him as a vessel for it's plans. It's the reason why Leopold starts building his own cathedral of flesh in new York</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's possible, though I suspect the actual answer is that the Eye of Hazmiel was meant to be an Eye of a Tzimisce Methusaleh.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Clan Novels aren't the best planned out things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-28-2022, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:02:56-07:00","id":1488302,"title":"","content":"I'd have to find where...but it was stated at the time the eye was just a tool used to use an antideluvian in the clan novel series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:06:23-07:00","id":1488303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488302#post1488302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to find where...but it was stated at the time the eye was just a tool used to use an antideluvian in the clan novel series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I recently re-read the books and the fact that Xavier thinks its an Anteduluvian is meant as dramatic irony. There's also never any overt links to the Tzimisce Antediluvian but Hazmiel wakes up in the end like A NIGHTMARE ON ELM STREET stinger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:08:39-07:00","id":1488304,"title":"","content":"I mean...it happens in new York and a pile of tzimisce powers. I find it FAR more likely it's the tzimisce antideluvian who is under new York then some ravnos Methuselah in India who also has that much visscitude and koldunic sorcery for some reason which makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:10:35-07:00","id":1488306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488304#post1488304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean...it happens in new York and a pile of tzimisce powers. I find it FAR more likely it's the tzimisce antideluvian who is under new York then some ravnos Methuselah in India who also has that much visscitude and koldunic sorcery for some reason which makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You find it more likely that the magical object directly linked to a Methuselah is channeling a random nearby Antediluvian than the actual person its linked to?<br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> That's fine but I have the view that there's nothing particularly weird about Out of Clan Disciplines for Ancients.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> There's also the fact Leopold isn't in New York when he's doing his horrific murders with Koldunic Sorcery and Vicissitude. He's in a cave in Hayesburg, which is in Connecticut. Yes, the Tzimisce Antediluvian is closer than, say, Augustus Giovanni, but why is he reaching 100 miles away to a random Tremere Neonate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-28-2022, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:13:23-07:00","id":1488307,"title":"","content":"That High? I don't know if a single example of THAT many clan specific powers and clan specific sorcery on a printed npc. Leopold doesn't use elder chimestry and I can not think of a single printed canon npc out of hundreds that has non tzimisce with koldunic sorcery. The clan isn't well known for teaching their secrets to outsiders.<br /> <br /> But as always, your table your canon lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:16:48-07:00","id":1488308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488307#post1488307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That High? I don't know if a single example of THAT many clan specific powers and clan specific sorcery on a printed npc. Leopold doesn't use elder chimestry and I can not think of a single printed canon npc out of hundreds that has non tzimisce with koldunic sorcery. The clan isn't well known for teaching their secrets to outsiders.<br /> <br /> But as always, your table your canon lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know he has Vicissitude but I should point out we don't actually know he's using Koldunic Sorcery either. It just looks like it because he's causing fire to leap out of the ground and lava. He could be using Chimestry or something completely unknown power wise.<br /> <br /> But I admit I stated that I thought they planned for Hazmiel to be a Tzimisce before they retconned him into a Ravnos.<br /> <br /> So I think it's compensating for a mistake in communication among writers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T21:45:37-07:00","id":1488319,"title":"","content":"Maybe it wasn't Vicissitude or Koldunic sorcery at all<br /> It could have been Chimestry<br /> Even at level 6, it makes terrible things<br /> Horrid Blade of the Demons create a dangerous weapon out of nothing<br /> Shared Nightmare/Mass Horror like Horrid Reality, except it affects multiple people (Horrid Reality: Places the mind of the victim in an illusionary world of the vampire's creation)<br /> <br /> At level 7<br /> Suspension of Disbelief: Make an illusion seem completely real or what is real seem unbelievable<br /> <br /> At level 9<br /> Mayaparisatya: Temporarily make an illusion completely real or alter a person or object that already exists, possibly even erasing them from existence<br /> Truths of the Universe: Make a created illusion permanently real<br /> <br /> Hazimel/The Rakshasa is/was a 4th generation child of Zapathasura, so safe to assume, his eye, witch he made an amulette, potentially could chanel his powers, if not all ,the signiture power of his clan at least, and even if you just take these publised powers and not some Elder made ones even those are capable of those things what Leopold did was described in the novels<br /> <br /> And of course, Leopold was Tremere Antitribu and insane (maybe even had the Eldest behind his eyes, or at least had vicissitude posioning, but something was not okay in his head), yes after the Gangrel incident, he later collected the remains of the defeated Gangrel and created a gargantuan sculpture stretched in every direction at every angle to almost fill a very sizable cavern nearby. The work was not only of stone; flesh and bone adorned the sculpture and were incorporated into it. Entombed within the work were kindred limbs, the bodies of a dozen or more, few completely intact, some still moving. Leopold considered that abomination to be his masterpiece and subsequently went into torpor for weeks.<br /> And this is in my humble oppinion a bit of a clue<br /> Shaped STONE and Flesh together.... Hazimel was a stonemanson<br /> Vampire bodies tend to start to decay after Final Death and those Gangrel died... the fact, it was writen like that, not to mention the moving part, suggest, at least in my oppinion, Leopold not used Vicissitude, but shaped reality with his insane mind fueled by Hazimel's 4th Gen power.<br /> <br /> While Leopold slept, Hesha Ruhadze took the Eye and left. Leopold woke up to find his &quot;vision&quot; was gone and began looking for it. Fortunately for him, he retained some of the powers of the ancient artifact and left for New York.<br /> This in my humble oppinion further supports, it was reality alteration, not vicissitude<br /> <br /> Well my two cents of course","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-29-2022, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T23:36:16-07:00","id":1488324,"title":"","content":"Could it be that the Eye just augments whichever Discipline the holder already has (or potentially has)? So a Tremere with Vicissitude in his blood might find his Tzimisce powers flourishing, while a Toreador might suddenly be throwing around Presence 9 powers and moving faster than light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T23:40:04-07:00","id":1488325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488324#post1488324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could it be that the Eye just augments whichever Discipline the holder already has (or potentially has)? So a Tremere with Vicissitude in his blood might find his Tzimisce powers flourishing, while a Toreador might suddenly be throwing around Presence 9 powers and moving faster than light?</div> </div> </div> </div>True but Leopold isn't even aware he's a Tremere Antitribu as he's been brainwashed into thinking he's a Toreador.<br /> <br /> Because the Clan novel are weird.<br /> <br /> <img src