 class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say Paths would still be effected because Hazimel's mind is what is fucking you up, not his generic evil but his whole values systems and consciousness.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm sure plenty of Sabbat would believe otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Besides, it's a great deterrent against PCs wanting to get a hold of the item <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:45:06-07:00","id":1488659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488299#post1488299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hazimel created the eye as gift to antideluvians to expand their domian. Hazimel didn't have tons of visscitude or kokdunic sorcery. It's far more likely that the Tzimisce Antideluvian tapped into the artifact when Leopold had it and why he was drawn to New York. Using him as a vessel for it's plans. It's the reason why Leopold starts building his own cathedral of flesh in new York</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading was similar, when the novels first came out. The Eldest was known to be in the state of New York and Hazimel was a complete cipher, so I concluded that the Eye was mirroring the Vicissitude and Koldunic Sorcery of the Eldest during the battle against the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos clan was loldeleted not long after, so it never mattered to me who Hazimel really was. The only noteworthy aftereffect of that battle was that it served as the justification for the Gangrel's departure from the Camarilla","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-01-2022, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T00:01:23-07:00","id":1488673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488659#post1488659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading was similar, when the novels first came out. The Eldest was known to be in the state of New York and Hazimel was a complete cipher, so I concluded that the Eye was mirroring the Vicissitude and Koldunic Sorcery of the Eldest during the battle against the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos clan was loldeleted not long after, so it never mattered to me who Hazimel really was. The only noteworthy aftereffect of that battle was that it served as the justification for the Gangrel's departure from the Camarilla</div> </div> </div> </div>Odd fact: Hazimel is explicitly confirmed to be one of the survivors of the Week of Nightmares. Presumably the oldest and most powerful Ravnos left.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T18:47:40-07:00","id":1488751,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Dark Ages V5 game where the Eye of Hazimel popped up in one of the PC's preludes. Much later, that PC, who's a Ravnos of Hazimel's lineage that used to be a Mage, discovered the following through a vision sent by Hazimel.<br /> <br /> The Eye of Hazimel is a living eye belonging to the Ravnos methuselah Hazimel (or, according to some, to Zapathasura himself). Before his embrace, Hazimel, a mage, symbolically removed his third eye and placed within it his avatar, thus preserving it.<br /> <br /> I'll note that I unabashedly alter things in the World of Darkness to suit the plot of whatever chronicle I'm running. For the chronicle I'm currently running, it essentially has plot device level power that granted Hazimel access to the powers he had as a mage before being embraced. So far I haven't defined what exact Arete rating it'd have, or Spheres that it'd grant access to, as it's been largely in the hands of NPCs. I'll probably have the method of replacing one of your own eyes with the Eye of Hazimel be one way to use it, but that using it this way has various negative effects on the user as seen in the canon World of Darkness. I'm still contemplating on how one might use the eye without suffering the negative side effects, but I've got a lot of time before I need to get that one figured out. For another chronicle, I might do something entirely different if I included the Eye of Hazimel as part of the story.<br /> <br /> Here's an excerpt from the scene I wrote for my Dark Ages v5 game that involved the Eye of Hazimel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDeception.\u201d The words, antediluvian Sanskrit brimming with fury, echo within your mind, startling you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A sudden and sharp audible snap fills the air of your vardo. A large crack has formed at the center of your vanity mirror. There\u2019s another audible snap and the crack spider webs across the mirror, splitting it into seven parts, seven images of you, each of which stares back with a third empty eye upon their brow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You blink and the images in the mirror change to that of a young man with ash-painted skin and matted dreadlocks resembling Lord Shiva, and a closed third eye upon his brow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The man\u2019s third eye opens, the mirror shatters, and you find yourself in the eye of a desert sandstorm, sitting lotus upon a rock across from the man you saw in the mirror, now adorned in the robes of a Sadhu and clad in six arms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cYou have been deceived. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>He</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> has deceived you. You, heir of my blood who is not my childe. See, now, the truth of your remaking, and the defiling of your and my avatara.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Iravati then sees a vision of her being embraced by Praveena, who\u2019s image flickers a moment before changing to that of Devadas, the Eye of Hazimel held in his left hand.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 08-01-2022, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T20:26:11-07:00","id":1488757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488269-eye-of-hazimel?p=1488751#post1488751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a Dark Ages V5 game where the Eye of Hazimel popped up in one of the PC's preludes. Much later, that PC, who's a Ravnos of Hazimel's lineage that used to be a Mage, discovered the following through a vision sent by Hazimel.<br /> <br /> The Eye of Hazimel is a living eye belonging to the Ravnos methuselah Hazimel (or, according to some, to Zapathasura himself). Before his embrace, Hazimel, a mage, symbolically removed his third eye and placed within it his avatar, thus preserving it.<br /> <br /> I'll note that I unabashedly alter things in the World of Darkness to suit the plot of whatever chronicle I'm running. For the chronicle I'm currently running, it essentially has plot device level power that granted Hazimel access to the powers he had as a mage before being embraced. So far I haven't defined what exact Arete rating it'd have, or Spheres that it'd grant access to, as it's been largely in the hands of NPCs. I'll probably have the method of replacing one of your own eyes with the Eye of Hazimel be one way to use it, but that using it this way has various negative effects on the user as seen in the canon World of Darkness. I'm still contemplating on how one might use the eye without suffering the negative side effects, but I've got a lot of time before I need to get that one figured out. For another chronicle, I might do something entirely different if I included the Eye of Hazimel as part of the story.<br /> <br /> Here's an excerpt from the scene I wrote for my Dark Ages v5 game that involved the Eye of Hazimel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDeception.\u201d The words, antediluvian Sanskrit brimming with fury, echo within your mind, startling you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A sudden and sharp audible snap fills the air of your vardo. A large crack has formed at the center of your vanity mirror. There\u2019s another audible snap and the crack spider webs across the mirror, splitting it into seven parts, seven images of you, each of which stares back with a third empty eye upon their brow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You blink and the images in the mirror change to that of a young man with ash-painted skin and matted dreadlocks resembling Lord Shiva, and a closed third eye upon his brow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The man\u2019s third eye opens, the mirror shatters, and you find yourself in the eye of a desert sandstorm, sitting lotus upon a rock across from the man you saw in the mirror, now adorned in the robes of a Sadhu and clad in six arms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cYou have been deceived. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>He</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> has deceived you. You, heir of my blood who is not my childe. See, now, the truth of your remaking, and the defiling of your and my avatara.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Iravati then sees a vision of her being embraced by Praveena, who\u2019s image flickers a moment before changing to that of Devadas, the Eye of Hazimel held in his left hand.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's very interesting! Regarding the Arete, if I were you I'd probably give 7+, given the legendary status of the artifact I'd also probably give high sphere levels as well to better portray it, likely master level in at least 3 spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:16:46-07:00","id":1488880,"title":"","content":"I read the theory somewhere back in the day that the Eye was originally the Eldest's, and Hazimel stole it. I liked that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}